error: Element `<button>` inside a for-loop needs a unique ID (event handlers or stateful classes such as `active:`) but has no `id` or `key` attribute.
         help: Add a `key={unique_value}` attribute so each iteration gets a unique ID:
                for item in &self.items { <button key={item.id} onClick={...}>...</button> }
         note: Elements in loops share the same source location, so the auto-generated ID
               would be identical across iterations, causing GPUI state conflicts.
               Use `key` for a composite auto-ID, or `id` to supply a fully custom ID.
 --> tests/ui/fragment_loop_missing_key.rs:5:34
